Package: vidwatcher
Version: 0.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: julecko <julkoklein@gmail.com>
Section: video
Priority: optional
Depends: ffmpeg, adduser, systemd
Description: Daemon that batch-converts videos to AV1 + Opus (WebM)
 vidwatcher watches a set of configured directories and periodically
 re-encodes new video files to AV1 video and Opus audio in a WebM
 container - a compact, royalty-free combination that plays natively on
 modern Android devices.
 .
 Conversion parameters, the scan interval and the watched directories are
 all set in /etc/vidwatcher/config.toml. A per-file state database keeps
 the daemon from re-converting the same video twice.
